               "text": "### Conclusion\n\nWe have learned two friendly new tables:\n\n- Multiplying by 6 means adding the number six times, which is the same as counting by sixes: 6, 12, 18, 24, 30...\n- Multiplying by 7 means adding the number seven times, which is the same as counting by sevens: 7, 14, 21, 28, 35...\n\nWe used a flower with six petals for the table of six, and the seven days of a week for the table of seven. We also saw that 6 × 7 = 42 and 7 × 6 = 42. Changing the order of the factors does not change the product. (<htcite0>)\n\nKeep practicing with real objects — count the petals of flowers by sixes, count the days of the weeks by sevens — and explore the interactive tables again. You will see that these two tables always work.",
